{
  "id": "halden-normal-operation",
  "title": "Halden: normal operation",
  "description": "Four fictional nuclear units at Halden run at full power on a summer night, with nothing scripted to happen. They export about 4.4 GW through one 420 kV switchyard, tied by three circuits each to Hasle and Tegneby, into the same Norwegian grid as the loss-of-offsite-power exercise. A rain shower drifts over the units from the southwest about 15 minutes in; weather is scenery here and does not change the Plants or the Grid. Use it to walk through the plants, the grid and the Assistant, or inject your own fault from a unit's Instructor actions.",
  "objectives": [
    "Walk through steady full-power operation: each unit's live display, the export of the four unit bays, the switchyard voltage and the loading of the Hasle and Tegneby circuits and the NO1 corridors (connection-points.list, power-flow.snapshot).",
    "Follow the grid frequency and the reserves in steady state; nothing in this Scenario is scheduled to disturb them.",
    "Watch the rain shower cross the complex and read the local weather at a unit or at the ground probe. Weather does not change Plant or Grid physics.",
    "Optionally inject a fault yourself, from a unit's Instructor actions or by opening a circuit in the grid panel, and follow the response."
  ],
